Important notes for the Dialog version:
---------------------------------------

Although this version was originally supposed to be a quick hack, because
i was nagging the author about a DLG CardGuppies, it is now a interim
version before the new and improved version will come out (I've got no
idea how long this will take, so we (me and the author) have decided to
put this one out to see what the reactions will be. One terrible bug from
the Xenolink version has been stomped (was a lost carrier bug which
destroyed the player files).

I suggest you might give this door a try. There will be no bugfixes for this
version, because a complete rewrite is on it's way.


Installation:

Copy all files in the archive to DOORS:CardGuppies-III and create a
menu entry like this:

[ 1] Letter:                   C
[ 2] Executable: (path/name)   DOORS:CardGuppies-III/CardGuppies-III "%NAME"
"%ALIAS" %LEVEL %PORT
[ 4] Description:              CardGuppies-III
[ 5] Type:                     Executable
[ 6] Help File:                DOORS/O
[ 7] Lower level:              1
[ 8] Upper level:              255
[ 9] Hidden:                   NO
[10] Load type:                OVERLAY
[11] Ask user if sure:         NO
[12] Pend messages:            YES
[13] Cli mode:                 NO
[14] Pause on completion:      NO
[15] Log value:                None
[16] Activity string:          Beats your score in CardGuppies !!!
[17] Priority:                 DEFAULT


- This is an exact port from the Xenolink version, done by the Xenolink 
author. In the meantime it is now longer compiled with Aztec, but with
SAS C. This means the keyfile for Xenolink still works under DLG.
(meaning only Alan Bland can install this game as a registered user).

- The unregistered version is extremely crippled (but still playable),
but i can assure you, the game is WORTH the shareware fee. 

- Shareware fees must be real CASH! (The author can't exchange many kinds
of checks and money orders, so he decided not to accept them anymore).

- The readme.sysop is still from the Xenolink version, but most of it is 
still valid.

- This is an interim version, put out to make some people happy :-). A
CardGuppies Pro is on it's way !!! (With more configurable features, 
multiple playing per day, built in editor for the sysop, much nicer intro
screens and every nice feature we can think of. This will make all Xeno
sysops jealous :-)). (Keyfiles will remain the same for all versions). The
Pro version unregistrated will also be somewhat less crippled than this one.

- Need any more ? Go ahead and try it! But remember: The registrated version
is always the best.

